yoyo agents now shows what an agent file's tools / disallowedTools actually turn into in yoyo, instead of echoing the raw Claude Code names. All checks pass (fmt, clippy with -D warnings, full cargo test with 7212 passed), and it's committed as ce98e25a.

What changed
• New `src/agent_tool_names.rs`. resolve_agent_tools maps Claude Code names to yoyo tools: Read→read_file, Write→write_file, Edit/MultiEdit→edit_file, Glob→list_files, Grep→search, Bash→bash, WebSearch→web_search, TodoWrite→todo. A yoyo tool name written directly maps to itself.
  • Matching is exact and case-sensitive, based on the wording in Claude Code's docs.
  • disallowedTools is applied first. An entry like Bash(git push *) removes the whole tool.
  • If tools is omitted, the agent gets every child tool minus the disallowed ones.
  • If tools is given and nothing in it resolves, the agent is marked not usable rather than given everything.
  • Entries that don't resolve are listed with a reason, never dropped silently.
• The child's tools are read from the real child tool build, not a copied list, so TodoWrite maps to todo but is reported as not available to sub-agents. A test checks that every mapping target is in BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES.
• `render_agent` in `src/agent_defs.rs` prints the resolved names, an unresolved: line, a note for whole-tool removals, and a not usable: line. I ran the built binary on a temporary repo with two agent files, and the output matched the tests.
• Left unmapped on purpose: Task/Agent (reason given: "nested delegation not supported yet"), plus WebFetch, NotebookEdit and MCP tool names ("no yoyo tool").

Positive control: I made the branch for omitted tools ignore disallowedTools, in one command that also restored it. Exactly one test failed, omitted_tools_means_all_available_minus_disallowed (11 passed, 1 failed). After restoring, all 12 pass and no marker is left in the file.

Outside the planned three files: src/agent_defs_tests.rs had a test pinned to the old raw tools: Read, Grep output, so I updated its expected string and added two full-output tests. I also added ARCHITECTURE.md entries for both files, recording the old raw-string behaviour as superseded. docs/src is unchanged: it never described the tools line, so nothing there became wrong.

On #1250: I posted the mapping table and the control result before the final checks, then a second comment with what landed and what's next: the agent dispatcher with a subagent_type parameter, the trust gate for project agent files, REPL /agents, and the user docs page.
